    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature for `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The endpoint pipeline already maps the request body to the `Owner` entity (`BuildOwner` \u2192 `toOwner`) and renders the response via MapStruct (`RespondWithOwner`/`...Created` \u2192 `toOwnerDto`), so the change was entirely in the model, the API contract, and the schema \u2014 no new function classes needed.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a stored `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, and a derived `@Transient getSalutation()`: returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is null/blank. This follows the existing derived-field pattern (`getDisplayName`, `getInitials`, etc.).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (optional input, documented as MR/MRS/MS/DR) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and `salutation` (`readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema. The build regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` and the MapStruct impl, which now maps `title` both ways and `salutation` onto the response DTO.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table. The tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the explicit DDL column was required for the JPA insert of `title` to work.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` creates an owner with `title=DR, lastName=who` and confirms `GET` returns `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`.\n\nKept it as a plain string (not an enum) so MapStruct's `OwnerFieldsDto`\u2192`Owner` mapping stays a trivial `String`\u2192`String` with no enum conversion to maintain.",
