    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the codebase's established conventions cleanly.\n\n- `Owner` already carries a family of `@Transient` derived display getters \u2014 `getDisplayName()`, `getInitials()`, `getMembershipNumber()`, `getCheckDigit()` \u2014 each documented as \"derived from the owner's own fields.\" The new `getSalutation()` lands right among them with matching Javadoc phrasing and the same `@Transient` + null/blank-guard style. Salutation is a pure function of `title` + `lastName`, so the entity is the natural home; no DTO or service duplication is introduced.\n- The stored `title` field is added alongside the other persisted columns (next to `email`) with a conventional getter/setter, cleanly separated from the derived getter.\n- Schema changes are mechanical and consistent across all four dialects (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres), each placing `title VARCHAR(10)`/`TEXT` in the same position.\n- OpenAPI is updated coherently: `title` as an input property and `salutation` as a `readOnly` derived property, mirroring how `initials`/`full_name` are already modeled.\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class or method is becoming a catch-all, and a maintainer would find this the obvious place for the logic.",
